# TLS_MODE=byo-cert — the operator brought the certificate (ADR-0090).
#
# For a company that already has a wildcard, or issues from its own internal CA, and does not want
# ACME anywhere near this box. Caddy serves the two files and never contacts an ACME directory, so
# this mode needs no ACME_EMAIL, no DNS token, and the **stock official caddy image**.
#
# The files are ./secrets/tls/{fullchain.pem,privkey.pem}, mounted read-only at /etc/caddy/tls.
# bootstrap.sh refuses to bring the stack up when either is missing or empty, rather than starting a
# Caddy that fails to load them. :80 stays published for the HTTP→HTTPS redirect, not for issuance.
#
# Renewal is the operator's: this deployment cannot renew a certificate it did not issue. Replace
# both files and reload Caddy — the step is in docs/deploy-runbook.md.
#
# TLS_MODE and DOMAIN come from ./secrets/caddy.env, written on the box by bootstrap.sh and never
# committed. The private key never leaves the box either.

{$DOMAIN} {
	tls /etc/caddy/tls/fullchain.pem /etc/caddy/tls/privkey.pem

	import /etc/caddy/Caddyfile.d/site.caddy
}
